{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ee24a0c5165633b1","type":"text","text":"==The division authority==","x":-147,"y":-34,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"151083674c73ae45","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Division X is led by a single handler. It’s their responsibility to train, organize and coordinate the division resources towards the eradication of any threats they deem pertinent to humanity's long term survival.","x":-420,"y":-400,"width":345,"height":220},
		{"id":"845a8d16824e4b90","type":"text","text":"Who will be in charge of you as a team depends of uncontrollable things that are not in the hands of the logistics branches, but instead of who is needed in a specific window of time at the correct time.\n\nOr who is available in specific moment, sometimes one has to do due with what it is given, such is the life of the hunter. ","x":160,"y":-420,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"38f0a0731be425b0","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> During character creation, players and the admin should discuss what kind of person the division’s handler is and choose one of the options below, gaining a small bonus according to their background.","x":-464,"y":-740,"width":433,"height":196},
		{"id":"d04cd80838f28491","type":"text","text":"For new operatives just getting experience, a single Representative managing them is an usual experience.\n\nfor those with enough experience to kill worms themselves, they are used to rotate between a selection of Representatives is not only usual but generally the norm for an Assault team.","x":164,"y":-757,"width":392,"height":213},
		{"id":"e3a6f2ca53c42dc5","type":"text","text":"Options for handlers are in page 4!\n\nChapter 1 is generally managed by Rafael Mondragon (represented by the handler \"Retired exorcist\")\n\nChapter 2 will rotate depending of pillars, so each option is connected to their specific guy in charge around!","x":-160,"y":-1280,"width":427,"height":241},
		{"id":"f85c1c702c39b3ad","type":"text","text":"==Mundane kits==","x":-147,"y":80,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0130efb80c31bcbc","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Have you ever wondered what happens when an exorcist isn’t on duty executing sins? Well, wonder no more! In Division X, exorcists are also part of everyday operations, helping the branch fulfill its function as a productive part of the organization known as CAIN. \n> \n> You can become a receptionist, accepting telephone calls and reassuring strangers nothing suspicious is happening inside the division. Or you can be the chauffeur, driving the handler or your fellow exorcists around when necessary, just don’t forget the keys ;)","x":-540,"y":280,"width":440,"height":371},
		{"id":"3ee5dbf4afebce28","type":"text","text":"Operatives once passed their Simulacrum training experience and are expected to work on populated locations, can request any kind of item needed to do a \"regular job\" if needed, to not only keep appearances with local population but to have a sense of \"normalcy\" back to their lives.\n\nThe Administration promises to find the best option or position related to their previous past experience before becoming a host to authorize and find a location appropriate to them to \"work\" in.","x":140,"y":300,"width":434,"height":284},
		{"id":"0c0242f8b6142dc0","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> At character creation, each player picks a mundane kit from the list on the right and adds it to their standard kit. During off-hours, exorcists can Clock In and work for the division in exchange for scrip. (See the Clock In action in the Off-hours section for more details).","x":-200,"y":1007,"width":423,"height":233},
		{"id":"390cf8a5785d9840","type":"text","text":"Options for this are present in page 5!","x":-640,"y":1094,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"faa42425194e98a3","type":"text","text":"==Awareness==","x":-460,"y":20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"05be9979c38a22cb","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Exorcists must deal with world's awareness of the supernatural. At the end of every hunt, decide how much awareness of the supernatural the actions of the exorcists and the sin generated as seen on the table below.","x":-1000,"y":-61,"width":399,"height":222},
		{"id":"41e2e808848530da","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Light== \n> \n> *A few witnesses, small collateral damage.* \n> \n> ==3d6==","x":-993,"y":-383,"width":385,"height":187},
		{"id":"98ea28d4f77dd46d","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Mild== \n> \n> *A dozen witnesses, noticeable collateral damage.* \n> \n> ==4d6==","x":-1540,"y":-52,"width":404,"height":204},
		{"id":"cfee9109d7c533a7","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Severe== \n> \n> *A crowd of witnesses, massive collateral damage.* \n> \n> ==5d6==","x":-974,"y":320,"width":347,"height":196},
		{"id":"3c00aa7ed21e8c47","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> At the start of a campaign, create a six part talisman titled ‘Awareness’.","x":-2040,"y":-5,"width":340,"height":110},
		{"id":"f9e8142fc8274d23","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> At the end of every hunt, roll dice according to how much awareness the exorcists generated as seen above. ==For each 4+, slash the talisman once.==","x":-2560,"y":-32,"width":360,"height":165},
		{"id":"88bfc2d54c7ee275","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> This ongoing talisman represents how close the mundane authorities, populace and other organizations are from discovering the existence of CAIN and supernatural creatures. Every time the Awareness Talisman is fully slashed, raise the Awareness Level by 1 (maximum of 2) and reset the talisman. If the talisman is fully slashed with an Awareness Level of 2, the division is shut down and CAIN deploys a full veil memory reset.","x":-2616,"y":-520,"width":472,"height":280},
		{"id":"f03947ad93618ee5","type":"text","text":"(Addendum: Rising awareness level does not mean early ending, but it allows me to use \"Special enemy types\" related to each chapter to deploy, so yeah is hell but a different kind of hell :3)","x":-2570,"y":-800,"width":381,"height":152},
		{"id":"2376a662338462d5","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Slashes on the Awareness Talisman can be removed during off-hours by doing a Cover Up action (See the Off-hours section for more details).","x":-2562,"y":300,"width":364,"height":169},
		{"id":"149d7d60cb463d3c","type":"text","text":"==CLEANUP JOBS==","x":-3040,"y":25,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"0b0b8272189bfdbd","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Awareness levels can only be removed between hunts by working on cleanup jobs instead of going to off-hours (this means the exorcists won’t have time to do any off-hours actions before being deployed for the next hunt)","x":-3580,"y":-58,"width":409,"height":216},
		{"id":"fa6635e9d17b4b6a","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> At the start of a Cleanup Job, the group must decide one type of activity from the list below and describe a detail that best mirrors the current fictional situation.","x":-3558,"y":-380,"width":366,"height":205},
		{"id":"963c9ca8468c6ac8","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> At the end of a successful cleanup job, reset the Awareness Talisman and decrease the Awareness Level by 1.","x":-4080,"y":-132,"width":369,"height":148},
		{"id":"d455596f57f88f0c","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==ASSAULT== \n> Do violence to a target \n> ==Detail:== The target of the attack. \n> ==Examples:== A trace’s den, a cultist hideout, a secret meeting spot used by binders.","x":-4620,"y":-152,"width":389,"height":189},
		{"id":"5ac6bc16d38ecdee","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==STEALTH== \n> Trespass unseen \n> ==Detail:== The goal of the covert action. ==Examples:== The evidence locker of a police station, the hard drive of a worried citizen.","x":-4660,"y":-520,"width":354,"height":215},
		{"id":"3755fd144adc8532","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==OCCULT== \n> Influence the psyche sea \n> ==Detail:== The arcane method. \n> ==Examples:== Deploy protective talismans, perform a dangerous ritual.","x":-4620,"y":200,"width":429,"height":190},
		{"id":"b77b3d33a6979294","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==SOCIAL== \n> Negotiate, bargain or threaten \n> ==Detail:== A suggestible individual. \n> ==Examples:== A journalist writing an exposé about the division, a neighbor willing to look the other way.","x":-4020,"y":200,"width":381,"height":207},
		{"id":"1a80d5ee44231de4","type":"text","text":"==CLOCK IN==","x":460,"y":1094,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1622a6e89773a1c7","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> You clock in and use one of your mundane kits to work, describe how you use one of your registered skills to do so. ==Roll the dice and gain a number of scrip according to the highest result==:\n> \n> 1-5: 1 script.\n> 6: 2 script.","x":920,"y":1009,"width":457,"height":230},
		{"id":"bd73f87c1c946c26","x":160,"y":20,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"==Off hours=="},
		{"id":"23b974ff10614ee9","x":660,"y":-61,"width":456,"height":223,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> During off-hours, each exorcist can take 2 off-hours actions from the list below. Exorcists that choose not to report their injuries or did not have any injuries can instead take 3 actions. Actions with the ==‘focus==’ stamp can only be taken once per exorcist per off-hours."},
		{"id":"0e47dfd2289cf061","x":1320,"y":21,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Options list are present in page 19!"}
	],
